From: HakiOS
Subject: [PATCH 0141] 0141 sweetshot: kernel screenshots into the log ring

What: a low-priority kernel thread in AppleCLCD point-samples the panel
memory (every sweetshot_div-th pixel and row, default 6: 1080x2400 -> 180x400),
converts to RGB565, PackBits-compresses over 16-bit words, FNV-1a-checksums it,
and writes it to the persistent log as base64 lines ("SWEET SHOT n begin ..." /
"SWEET SHOT n SEQ4 ..." / "SWEET SHOT n end"), which tools/sweet-shot.py (A4)
reassembles into a PNG. Boot-args: sweetshot=N seconds between timer shots
(0 = off), sweetshot_max shots a boot (default 8), sweetshot_div the sample
step. The freeze probe (next to sweet_freeze_dump) and Vol+ and Vol- held
together (SweetHIDButtons::key) also ask for a shot, so the thread runs even
with sweetshot=0. Buffers are IOMallocData/IOFreeData; the thread never takes
fLock and skips while fPowerOff or fPixels == 0.

Why: there is no way to see the screen during an unattended run (the 750
layout was never seen). The panel memory is readable by the kernel, so a
small picture can go into the log ring.

Proof: the log line "SWEET SHOT: every N s, max M, div D, panel WxH" once at
start, and "SWEET SHOT 1 begin ..." / "SWEET SHOT 1 end" around each shot.
---
